  "interpretation": {
    "silentHealing": "The 131,072-operation silent-heal workload is 30.1% and 51.6% slower than retained v0.36 (11.08/12.77 ms versus 8.51/8.42 ms). This is the first profiling target.",
    "ordinary": "Ordinary positive healing is 3.2% and 18.1% slower; full refills are 4.6% and 12.8% slower. Refused calls are 26.2% and 44.5% slower, but the absolute difference is only 0.09/0.16 ms per 131,072 calls.",
    "retainedMemory": "Used batches measure identical retained bytes per Actor in both runs at 1,024 and 4,096 Actors. Unused batches differ by 0–0.125 byte per Actor. Whole retained native Actor/stat state is approximately 11,336 bytes per Actor; this is not the size of the recovery module.",
    "variability": "Proc and world-update medians show 0.4–0.7% overhead in the first run and 11.1–23.8% in the second. Sealed clipping changes ranking. These runs do not isolate the cause or establish stable whole-world overhead; retain both and investigate instead of choosing a favorable result.",
    "next": "Profile silent healing on isolated fresh processes. Preserve callback order, live method selection and all prior native observations. Do not add per-Actor caches or replace storage without measured benefit."
  },
